[al:新概念英语第三册]
[ti:46. Do It Yourself]
[00:00.380] Passage 46 | 第46篇
[00:02.300] Do it yourself. | 自己动手。
[00:05.050] So great is our passion for doing things for ourselves, | 我们自己动手做事情的热情如此之高，
[00:09.730] that we are becoming increasingly less dependent on specialized labor. | 以至于我们越来越不依赖专业劳工。
[00:14.030] No one can plead ignorance of a subject any longer. | 再没有人能以对某一学科一无所知为由而推诿了。
[00:17.470] For there are countless do-it-yourself publications. | 因为有无数关于自己动手的出版物。
[00:21.145] Armed with the right tools and materials, | 备齐了合适的工具和材料，
[00:24.150] newlyweds gaily embark on the task of decorating their own homes. | 新婚夫妇愉快地着手装饰自己的家园。
[00:28.550] Men of all ages spend hours of their leisure time, | 各年龄段的男士们都把闲暇时间花在
[00:31.695] installing their own fireplaces, laying out their own gardens, | 安装自己的壁炉，布置自己的花园，
[00:35.730] building garages, and making furniture. | 建造车库和制作家具上。
[00:39.370] Some really keen enthusiasts, | 有些真正热衷的爱好者，
[00:42.210] go so far as to build their own record players and radio transmitters. | 甚至自己动手制作唱机和无线电发射器。
[00:46.800] Shops cater for the do-it-yourself craze, | 商店迎合这种自己动手的热潮，
[00:50.105] not only by running special advisory services for novices, | 不仅为新手提供专门的咨询服务，
[00:54.315] but by offering consumers bits and pieces which they can assemble at home. | 还向消费者提供可以在家组装的零配件。
[00:59.495] Such things provide an excellent outlet for pent-up creative energy. | 这种事情为被压抑的创造性精力提供了一个绝佳的宣泄口。
[01:04.080] But unfortunately, | 但不幸的是，
[01:05.740] not all of us are born handymen. | 我们并非所有人生来就是巧匠。
[01:08.780] Wives tend to believe that their husbands are infinitely resourceful and versatile. | 妻子们往往相信她们的丈夫足智多谋，多才多艺。
[01:14.575] Even husbands who can hardly drive a nail in straight, | 即使是那些连钉子都钉不直的丈夫，
[01:17.840] are supposed to be born electricians, carpenters, plumbers, and mechanics. | 也被认为是天生的电工、木匠、管道工和机械师。
[01:22.915] When lights fuse, furniture gets rickety, | 当灯泡烧坏了，家具摇摇晃晃了，
[01:26.100] pipes get clogged, or vacuum cleaners fail to operate, | 管道堵塞了，或者吸尘器坏了，
[01:29.940] wives automatically assume that their husbands will somehow put things right. | 妻子们就会理所当然地认为，她们的丈夫总会把事情搞定。
[01:35.295] The worst thing about the do-it-yourself game, | 自己动手这件事最糟糕的地方在于，
[01:38.650] is that sometimes husbands live under the delusion that they can do anything, | 有时丈夫们会自欺欺人地认为他们无所不能，
[01:42.915] even when they have been repeatedly proved wrong. | 即使他们已被屡次证明是错的。
[01:46.285] It is a question of pride as much as anything else. | 这更多的是一个面子问题。
[01:50.190] Last spring, | 去年春天，
[01:52.040] my wife suggested that I call in a man to look at our lawn mower. | 我妻子建议我请人来检查一下我们的割草机。
[01:56.315] It had broken down the previous summer, | 它在去年夏天就坏了，
[01:59.200] and though I promised to repair it, | 尽管我答应要修好它，
[02:01.270] I had never got round to it. | 但我一直没动手。
[02:03.435] I would not hear of the suggestion, | 我根本不听这个建议，
[02:05.825] and said that I would fix it myself. | 说我自己会把它修好。
[02:07.955] One Saturday afternoon, I hauled the machine into the garden, | 一个星期六下午，我把机器拖到花园里，
[02:11.810] and had a close look at it. | 仔细地检查起来。
[02:13.555] As far as I could see, it only needed a minor adjustment, | 就我看来，它只需要稍微调整一下，
[02:17.405] a turn of a screw here, | 这里拧一下螺丝，
[02:19.320] a little tightening up there, | 那里紧固一下，
[02:21.380] a drop of oil, | 再滴几滴油，
[02:22.710] and it would be as good as new. | 就会焕然一新。
[02:25.095] Inevitably, the repair job was not quite so simple. | 不出所料，维修工作并不那么简单。
[02:29.470] The mower firmly refused to mow. | 割草机就是不肯工作。
[02:32.850] So I decided to dismantle it. | 于是我决定把它拆开。
[02:35.855] The garden was soon littered with chunks of metal which had once made up a lawn mower. | 花园里很快就散落着一堆堆曾经组成割草机的金属碎片。
[02:41.175] But I was extremely pleased with myself. | 但我对自己非常满意。
[02:43.710] I had traced the cause of the trouble: | 我找到了故障的原因：
[02:45.800] one of the links in the chain that drives the wheels had snapped. | 驱动轮的链条上有一个链节断了。
[02:50.310] After buying a new chain, | 买了一条新链条后，
[02:52.487] I was faced with the insurmountable task of putting the confusing jigsaw puzzle together again. | 我面临着一个难以克服的任务：把这个令人困惑的拼图游戏重新组装起来。
[02:58.315] I was not surprised to find that the machine still refused to work after I had reassembled it, | 我重新组装好后，发现机器仍然拒绝工作，这并不奇怪，
[03:04.035] for the simple reason that I was left with several curiously shaped bits of metal, | 原因很简单，我剩下了一些形状奇特的金属碎片，
[03:09.365] which did not seem to fit anywhere. | 它们似乎哪里都安不上。
[03:12.410] I gave up in despair. | 我绝望地放弃了。
[03:15.115] The weeks passed, | 几周过去了，
[03:17.040] and the grass grew. | 草长高了。
[03:19.270] When my wife nagged me to do something about it, | 当我妻子催促我采取行动时，
[03:22.255] I told her that either I would have to buy a new mower, | 我告诉她，要么我得买一台新割草机，
[03:25.910] or let the grass grow. | 要么就让草继续长。
[03:28.475] Needless to say, our house is now surrounded by a jungle. | 不用说，我们的房子现在被一片“丛林”包围着。
[03:32.595] Buried somewhere in deep grass, | 埋在深草的某个地方，
[03:36.065] there is a rusting lawn mower, | 有一台生锈的割草机，
[03:38.615] which I have promised to repair, one day. | 我曾答应总有一天会把它修好。